  "editor": "QA WF CL03 Active Deactivate @ Tickets · Layout All layouts · Departments QA AO Dept B, QA RT19 WF Dept Change Add Description WHEN This rule will be executed when a record in Tickets is created. EXECUTE BASED ON A Record Action Run when a record is created, modified, or deleted. Create Edit Create or Edit Delete Field Changed A Date-Time field Run a fixed time before/after a date field on the record. A Ticket Event Run when a customer replies, an agent responds, a comment is added or a rating comes in. RULE MODE Recurring Fires every time a save matches the criteria. One time Fires at most once per record, even if the record is later updated and still matches. Done CONDITION 1 1 ⁨Subject⁩ starts with ⁨\"QA WF CL03 \"⁩ 2 ⁨Priority⁩ = ⁨High⁩ 3 ⁨Classification⁩ = ⁨Problem⁩ 4 ⁨Channel⁩ = ⁨Email⁩ Criteria Pattern (1 and ((2 and 3) or 4)) Which Tickets would you like to apply this rule to? Tickets matching certain conditions All Tickets 1 Subject starts with • 2 Priority is High • 3 Classification is Problem • 4 Channel is Email Criteria Pattern ( 1 and ((2 and 3) or 4) ) Edit Pattern Done ACTION Instant actions Run as soon as the rule fires. Field Update Configure inline Use a saved action Updates fields on the current record (the one that triggered the rule) before it's saved. QA NDC Agency code = Add field Add action Field Update Set fields on the current record. Owner Assignment Set the record owner. Webhook POST/PUT/PATCH to an external URL. Email Send an email via the platform email service. Task Create a task assigned to a user. Create Record Create a record in any module. Add Tags Apply tags to the triggering record. Remove Tags Take tags off the triggering record. Send happiness email Email the ticket's customer the Customer Happiness rating link. Update related record Set fields of the record this one links to, such as the ticket's contact or account. Add comment Post a comment on the ticket as the system, private to agents or visible to the contact. Send email reply Email a reply from the ticket's channel to the contact or to other addresses. Add followers Make agents follow the ticket so they get its updates. Mark as spam Move the ticket to spam, and optionally block its contact. Share ticket Share the ticket with another department. Add skills Add skills to the ticket, from the skills its module offers. Remove skills Take skills off the ticket. Recalculate skills Add the skills whose criteria match the ticket and remove those that no longer match. Re",
